- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } dphy_errors_0[16:16];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_15";
            desc = "Protocol violation interrupt in the device error reporting. When the expected EoTp or BTA sequence after the read command is not received, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_15[15:15];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_14";
            desc = "The reserved bit in the device error reporting. This bit is cleared when it is read. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_14[14:14];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_13";
            desc = "Bit of the invalid transmission length in the device error reporting. When the received data length is inconsistent with the expected one, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_13[13:13];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_12";
            desc = "Bit indicating an invalid DSI VC ID in the device error reporting. When the device receives an unidentified ID, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_12[12:12];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_11";
            desc = "\"DSI Data Type Not Recognized\" bit in the device error reporting. When the device receives an unrecognized data type, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_11[11:11];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_10";
            desc = "\"Checksum Error\" bit in the device error reporting. When the received data has cyclic redundancy check (CRC) errors, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_10[10:10];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_9";
            desc = "Multi-bit ECC error in the device error reporting. When the device receives data which has multi-bit CRC errors, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_9[9:9];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_8";
            desc = "Single-bit ECC error in the device error reporting. When the device receives data which has single-bit CRC errors, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_8[8:8];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_7";
            desc = "Contention detected bit in the device error reporting. When the device has LP contention, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
- 0: No interrupt is generated.
- 1: An interrupt is generated. (data sheet access type RC)";
            sw = r; hw = w; onread = rclr;
            reset = 0x0;
        } ack_with_err_7[7:7];
        field {
            name = "ack_with_err_6";
            desc = "False control error in the device error reporting. When the device receives incorrect status sequence, an error is reported. This bit is cleared when it is read.
